The plan of record is clear: land the A+B+D bundle as 0.11.499. Locating the implementation sites — the P15-REL-ABORT release-worker spin, existing PR IN infrastructure, and the HB writer:
All pieces surveyed. Now implementing the bundle as 0.11.499. Checking the last plumbing details — self-fence reason enum, dlm_caw callback fields, and how the unlock rc propagates to v5:
rc propagates cleanly to the v5 wrapper — that's the hook point. Reading the self-fence enum and the v5 unlock wrapper:
Relay boundary reached — this session was orientation and site survey for the A+B+D bundle. Capturing the implementation-ready findings in the handoff before stopping:
Stopping at the relay boundary. Session 277 summary:

**This session completed the full implementation survey for the sess276-ruled A+B+D fix bundle (fenced-victim self-withdraw + BAST backoff + HB-stall instrumentation) and wrote a type-ready plan into the handoff. No code landed yet.**

Key findings, each verified by reading the code:

- **The victim-noncontainment root is a one-line errno mask:** `mxfs_pal_bdev_compare_and_write` collapses every non-good SCSI status — including RESERVATION CONFLICT — to `-EIO`, so a fenced node's CAW writes never look like fencing to any layer above.
- **The periodic PR self-check only exists on the TCP transport** — it lives inside `v5_tcp_death_worker_fn`, which is only created in the TCP mount branch. CAW mounts (the rig's transport) have no PR self-check at all.
- **Read-based fence detection provably cannot work here:** the incident victim's reads were 51 generations stale, so its heartbeat re-read kept showing its own record — exactly why the ruling demands target-generated PR IN state.
- **Most of hard-withdraw already exists:** `mxfs_disklock_withdraw` already refuses to stamp a foreign-owned slot (zero media writes), and `mxfs_v5_dlm_shutdown_withdraw` already fences acquires, stops the heartbeat, freezes grants, and stops discovery.
- All hook points for the new plumbing are identified with line numbers: the unlock-rc propagation path for conflict counting, the self-fence reason enum, the P15 re-arm sites for backoff, the PAL thread handle for the watchdog stack dump, and SG_IO/scsi_execute precedents for the new PR IN READ FULL STATUS call.

Criteria not met: 34 ledgered defects remain open, the fix bundle is unlanded, and the rig is still wedged from the sess276 incident — MXFS is not production ready. Next session: type the bundle per the handoff plan, build 0.11.499, write the four owed ledger entries, re-prep the cluster, and run the board.

